    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d809">

                <pb facs="1027" n="925" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg925"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/940: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hibbard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-03-07T12:00:00-00:44">March 7,
                            1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 9:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4. Firestone had his first conference with the President March 5. It was merely a
                    courtesy call and there was no discussion of current problems. Next conference
                    will be March 11 when supplementary agreement<anchor n="10" xml:id="d809-f1"/>
                    will be taken up.</p>
                <p>Strongly organized opposition party held national convention yesterday when
                    ex-President King was unanimously chosen to run against Barclay.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hibbard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d809-f1" n="10" xml:id="d809-f1-content">
                <p>i. e., agreement supplementary to the Loan Agreement of 1926, for text of which
                    see <ref target="frus1926v02#pg_574">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1926, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 574</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
